Subject: illumos: find runtime GC roots through /proc/<pid>/path

findRuntimeRoots() reads /proc/<pid>/{exe,cwd,fd/*,maps,environ}, the Linux
procfs layout. On illumos every nix-store --gc / --print-dead / --query
--roots aborted with

  error: filesystem error: read_symlink: File name too long [/proc/0/cwd]

because /proc/<pid>/cwd is a symlink whose readlink(2) returns 0 bytes (any
buffer size), which libstdc++'s read_symlink reports as ENAMETOOLONG, and
readProcLink() rethrows everything but ENOENT/EACCES/ESRCH. Also, fd/N are not
symlinks (readlink: EINVAL), exe/maps/environ do not exist.

illumos exposes the same information as readable symlinks under
/proc/<pid>/path/: a.out, cwd, root, one entry per open fd and one per mapped
object. Walk that directory under __sun, and have readProcLink() skip
ENAMETOOLONG/EINVAL entries instead of aborting the whole root scan. The
process environment is not scanned on illumos (no /proc/<pid>/environ).

--- a/src/libstore/gc.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/gc.cc
@@ -319,7 +319,12 @@
     } catch (std::filesystem::filesystem_error & e) {
         if (e.code() == std::errc::no_such_file_or_directory
                 || e.code() == std::errc::permission_denied
-                || e.code() == std::errc::no_such_process)
+                || e.code() == std::errc::no_such_process
+                /* illumos: readlink(2) of /proc/<pid>/cwd returns 0 bytes, which
+                   libstdc++ reports as ENAMETOOLONG; /proc/<pid>/fd/N are not
+                   symlinks (EINVAL). Neither is a root; skip them. */
+                || e.code() == std::errc::filename_too_long
+                || e.code() == std::errc::invalid_argument)
             return;
         throw;
     }
@@ -359,6 +364,29 @@
